# Server access (prod)

Owner wants the agent to **use SSH key access** for health checks, logs, docker status, and analysis — without asking for a password each time.

## Connect (Windows / this machine)

| | |
|--|--|
| Host | `161.104.46.236` |
| User | `root` |
| Key | `C:\Users\Dir\.ssh\id_ed25519` (comment `dir_61@bk.ru`) |
| Alias | `ssh bervinov` (from `~/.ssh/config`) |
| App dir | `/opt/bervinov-academy` |
| Site | `https://academy.bervinov-miron.ru` |

```bash
ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i C:/Users/Dir/.ssh/id_ed25519 root@161.104.46.236 "COMMAND"
```

Or OpenSSH alias: `ssh bervinov "COMMAND"`.

From Python (paramiko): load `Ed25519Key` from `id_ed25519`, **no password**, `look_for_keys=False`.

## Auth rules

- Prefer **publickey only**. Do not store or reuse root passwords in rules/scripts/chat.
- If key auth fails, say so and ask the user — do not invent credentials.
- Never commit private keys or dump them into the repo / chat.
- Destructive ops (`full-restart`, wipe volumes, disable SSH password) only with explicit user OK.

## Typical checks

```bash
free -h; uptime; df -h /
cd /opt/bervinov-academy && docker compose ps
docker stats --no-stream
curl -sS -m 5 http://127.0.0.1:18080/health/
```

External: `https://academy.bervinov-miron.ru/health/`
